THOUGHT: The field `spawnpoints` is annotated `@Nullable`, but `getSpawnPoints()` has a non-null return type and is used assuming non-null (e.g., `isEmpty()`, `size()`). The safest fix is to ensure `getSpawnPoints()` never returns null by lazily initializing `spawnpoints` to an empty `ArrayList` when it’s null. This avoids changing public API annotations and won’t affect other errors. I’ll modify the method accordingly and then run the build to confirm that the specific NullAway error is gone and no new ones are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '103,107c\  @Override
  public List<Spawnpoint> getSpawnPoints() {
    if (this.spawnpoints == null) {
      this.spawnpoints = new ArrayList<>();
    }

    return this.spawnpoints;
  }
' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/environment/EntitySpawner.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway:|error: \[NullAway\]" -n new_build_output.log | head && tail -n 20 new_build_output.log
```

